    40|// -------------------------------------------------------------------
    41|// FATAL ERROR SHIELD — THIS IS THE BLACK SCREEN FIX.
    42|//
    43|// React error boundaries only catch errors thrown during RENDER. An error
    44|// thrown from a timer, an event handler, a native callback or any async
    45|// continuation never reaches them.
    46|//
    47|// React Native routes those to ErrorUtils' global handler. When it is invoked
    48|// with isFatal=true, the DEFAULT handler tears down the JS context. The Android
    49|// Activity stays alive, so the system status bar and navigation bar keep
    50|// drawing — but the React root view is emptied. The result is a black content
