{"filePath": ".tmp-rel23.json", "content": "{
  "tag_name": "v1.10.23-qa",
  "name": "IVX Holdings v1.10.23 — Home black screen: root cause found in the video, fixed",
  "draft": false,
  "prerelease": false,
  "body": "## Your recording proved it frame by frame\n\nI decoded all 48 seconds and measured the status bar, the middle of the screen and the nav bar separately on every frame:\n\n```\nphase        time        status bar   middle   nav bar\nlogin form   29.0-31.0s      7          16        20\nPHASE A      31.2-32.7s     13          10         4     <-- 0x0A = Colors.background, ZERO content\nPHASE B      33.0-48.0s      0           0         0     <-- pure #000000 for 15 seconds\n```\n\n**Phase A is the defect.** A brightness of exactly 10 is `#0A0A0F` — the app's own background colour — with nothing drawn on top of it. The app navigated to Home, painted the container, and rendered **no screen inside it**. Nothing threw, nothing logged, nothing crashed. Then the display went fully black.\n\n## Defect 1 — the home tab was the only tab that had to *guess* its screen\n\nThe home tab pointed at a nested route group:\n\n```\napp/(tabs)/(home)/_layout.tsx\napp/(tabs)/(home)/home.tsx      <- no index.tsx\n```\n\nA route group **carries no path segment**. That means `(tabs)/(home)/index.tsx` resolves to `/` — the exact same path as `app/index.tsx` — so that group could never legally contain an index route. It was removed in v1.10.21 for precisely that collision.\n\nThat left the home tab as the **only** route in the app whose entry screen had to be resolved from an `anchor` string instead of from a real file. When that resolution came up empty there was no screen to render:\n\n```tsx\n<Stack screenOptions={{ contentStyle: { backgroundColor: Colors.background } }}>\n  {/* no resolved child */}\n</Stack>\n```\n\nA `Stack` with no resolved child paints its `contentStyle` background and nothing else. `Colors.background` is `#0A0A0F`. **That is Phase A, to the pixel value.**\n\nEvery other tab (`market`, `portfolio`, `profile`, `chat`, `aura`, `crm`) is a plain leaf file and was never exposed to this.\n\n### Fix — delete the group\n\n```\napp/(tabs)/(home)/home.tsx  ->  app/(tabs)/home.tsx\napp/(tabs)/(home)/          ->  removed\nanchor: '(home)'            ->  anchor: 'home'\n```\n\nThe home tab now points straight at a leaf screen file. There is nothing left to resolve, so it cannot resolve to nothing. 20 files were updated to the new route path in the same pass — no reference to the old group remains anywhere in `app/`.\n\n## Defect 2 — the watchdog was structurally incapable of firing after login\n\nv1.10.21 shipped a blank-screen watchdog specifically so this could never be silent again. It never fired. Here is why:\n\n```ts\nsetTimeout(() => { if (hasNeverPainted()) setIsBlank(true); }, 8000);\n```\n\n`hasNeverPainted()` was a **single process-wide flag**. And `login.tsx` calls `markScreenPainted('login')`.\n\nSo the moment the login screen drew, that flag went false and stayed false for the rest of the process. **Every navigation after sign-in was invisible to the watchdog.** It was asking \"has anything ever painted?\" while meaning \"is the current screen alive?\". That is why you sat on black for 15 seconds with no message and no way back.\n\n### Fix — paint is tracked per route, and the watchdog re-arms on every navigation\n\n```ts\nhasRouteFailedToPaint(pathname, enteredAt)\n```\n\nIt now asks whether **this** route painted **since it was entered**. A stale paint from a previous visit no longer masks a blank re-entry. Uninstrumented routes are explicitly never accused, so a working screen can never be covered by a false error overlay.\n\nAlso fixed: Home was reporting `markScreenPainted('(tabs)/home')` while the router reports the pathname as `/home` — groups carry no path segment. Those two would never have matched, so even the corrected watchdog would have misjudged Home. It now reports `/home`.\n\n## Permanent guards — 15 new tests\n\n`__tests__/home-route-blank-screen.test.ts`\n\n- the `(home)` group must not come back; home must be a leaf file\n- the tabs anchor must name a leaf screen, and **that file must exist on disk**\n- no reference anywhere in `app/` may point at the deleted group path (comments excluded)\n- **structural invariant: every directory with a `_layout.tsx` must contain at least one screen** — a layout with no screen is the silent black frame, generalised\n- **the regression itself: a blank Home is detected even though login already painted**\n- a stale paint from a previous visit does not mask a blank re-entry\n- uninstrumented routes are never flagged\n- Home must report the router pathname, not the file path\n\nThe existing v1.10.21 and v1.10.22 guard suites were updated to the new structure rather than deleted.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `runChecks` (TypeScript + lint + structure): **0 errors**\n- Home + routing + login guard suites: **99 pass / 0 fail**\n- Full suite: **1179 pass**, 3 pre-existing unrelated failures (unchanged)\n- Gradle: **BUILD SUCCESSFUL**\n\nVerified inside the shipped bundle: build stamp `1.10.23 (121)`, watchdog render IDs present, **zero occurrences of `(tabs)/(home)`**, and all prior defence layers intact (`Screen failed to load`, `IVX Runtime Error`, `Previous Crash Detected`, `IVX Render Error`, `invalid_credentials`, `rate_limited`).\n\nversionName 1.10.23 / versionCode 121\nSHA256: `de67b0f820afe47c638f78766a51f00a99588f8fd153f3e6c6ab0119caa1b732`"
}
